WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.596
The industrial DMZ is commonly described as Level 3.

00:00:03.596 --> 00:00:04.246
5.

00:00:04.246 --> 00:00:08.130
It is a security extension to the traditional Purdue discussion,

00:00:08.130 --> 00:00:10.072
not an original numbered level.

00:00:10.072 --> 00:00:14.732
Its purpose is to create a controlled buffer between enterprise IT and

00:00:14.732 --> 00:00:19.393
site operations so ordinary enterprise systems do not communicate directly with control

00:00:19.393 --> 00:00:20.043
networks.

00:00:20.043 --> 00:00:23.150
Services in the industrial DMZ mediate necessary exchange.

00:00:23.150 --> 00:00:27.034
A jump host can provide a managed path for administration.

00:00:27.034 --> 00:00:30.918
A remote-access broker can enforce identity, approval, and session controls.

00:00:30.918 --> 00:00:35.191
Patch and antivirus repositories can stage content before it enters OT.

00:00:35.191 --> 00:00:39.851
Data replication services can move historian information outward without allowing enterprise clients

00:00:39.851 --> 00:00:41.793
to query control systems directly.

00:00:41.793 --> 00:00:44.124
Monitoring, logging, authentication proxies, file-transfer services,

00:00:44.124 --> 00:00:47.619
and update gateways may also belong in this zone.

00:00:47.619 --> 00:00:53.057
The exact design depends on operations, but each service should have a narrow purpose.

00:00:53.057 --> 00:00:56.941
Connections should specify approved sources, destinations, protocols, direction, and owner.

00:00:56.941 --> 00:01:01.213
Broad routing through the DMZ defeats the reason for having it.

00:01:01.213 --> 00:01:03.544
The DMZ is not automatically trusted.

00:01:03.544 --> 00:01:08.204
It faces connections from two environments and may contain high-value access services.

00:01:08.204 --> 00:01:11.700
Harden systems, separate administrative access, monitor traffic, patch deliberately,

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:16.361
retain logs, and avoid using the zone as a general-purpose server network.

00:01:16.361 --> 00:01:21.798
Remote sessions should terminate or be proxied there rather than passing transparently into OT.

00:01:21.798 --> 00:01:26.459
A strong industrial DMZ reduces direct enterprise-to-control connectivity and creates inspection points

00:01:26.459 --> 00:01:28.401
for data and control flows.

00:01:28.401 --> 00:01:33.838
It cannot repair weak segmentation below Level 3 or poor identity governance above it.

00:01:33.838 --> 00:01:39.664
Think of it as one architectural layer in a broader defense that includes controlled pathways,

00:01:39.664 --> 00:01:41.860
least privilege, asset knowledge, and operational oversight.
